// Plugin: no-inline-optimistic-in-surface
// Severity: warn
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Catches:    `<qc>.cancelQueries(...)` or `<qc>.setQueryData(...)` — the
//             optimistic-mutation plumbing dance happening inline at the JSX
//             composition layer (surfaces).
//
// Rationale:  Surfaces compose JSX; the cancel/snapshot/setQueryData/revert/
//             invalidate dance is data-layer work and belongs in
//             `features/<x>/hooks/*.ts` (or, when the shape fits, behind
//             `optimisticOptions({...})` from `features/_shared/use-optimistic-mutation.ts`).
//             Inline optimistic plumbing drifts subtly per surface — the
//             cancellation step gets skipped in one place, the revert in
//             another — and the bugs only surface under refetch races.
//
// Skips:      The plugin fires on ALL files matching biome's includes; the
//             intent ("surfaces only") is a path-scoping question that Biome
//             2.4.x can't express in `overrides` (tracking:
//             github.com/biomejs/biome/issues/6851). For now:
//               • `features/<x>/hooks/*.ts` — hooks LEGITIMATELY inline the
//                 pattern when tRPC's wide TInput inference trips the helper's
//                 narrower TInput. See `features/characters/hooks/use-star-toggle.ts`
//                 for the documented exception.
//               • Test files — assertion against the query cache is fine.
//             Both currently rely on per-line suppressions.
//
// Suppress:   // biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-inline-optimistic-in-surface: <reason>
//             (pair with a `hooks/` extraction TODO if the suppression is for
//             a surface site)
//
// Refs:       src/client/AGENTS.md §6
//             features/_shared/use-optimistic-mutation.ts (the helper)
//             features/characters/hooks/use-star-toggle.ts (the wide-TInput exception)
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// GritQL note: `$qc.<method>($args)` matches member-call syntax. `$qc` is the
// receiver (typically `queryClient` but also handles aliases like `qc` /
// `client`). The `as $call` span anchor highlights the whole call.

language js

or {
  `$qc.cancelQueries($args)` as $call,
  `$qc.setQueryData($args)` as $call
} where {
  // This rule is "in-SURFACE" by name and intent: optimistic plumbing in a SURFACE
  // is the smell; in a hook it's exactly where it belongs (AGENTS.md §6). Fire only
  // on surface files (biome-2.4 $filename guard) so hooks aren't false-flagged.
  $filename <: r".*/features/[^/]+/surfaces/.*",
  register_diagnostic(span=$call, message="Optimistic-mutation plumbing (`cancelQueries` / `setQueryData`) belongs in `features/<x>/hooks/`, not a surface. Surfaces compose JSX; data plumbing drifts when it lives at the call site. Use `optimisticOptions({queryClient, queryKey, merge, invalidateOnSettled})` from `features/_shared` (AGENTS.md §6), OR extract a hook that wraps the inline pattern (the wide-TInput tRPC exception — see `use-star-toggle.ts`).", severity="error")
}
